hin_succ_of_adj` might still lead to type mismatches related to the edge direction. The correct edge is from `w` to `x`, not `x` to `w`.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"replace_file_content","args":{"AllowMultiple":"false","Description":"\"Fix induction step and nil case in mem_ballWithin_of_walk_reverse\"","EndLine":"43","Instruction":"\"Fix nil and cons cases in mem_ballWithin_of_walk_reverse\"","ReplacementContent":"\"lemma mem_ballWithin_of_walk_reverse {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V] (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj]\\n    {v w : V} (q : G.Walk w v) : w ∈ GraphCalc.ballWithin G q.length v := by\\n  induction q with\\n  | nil =>\\n    dsimp [GraphCalc.ballWithin]\\n    exact Finset.mem_singleton_self _\\n  | cons hadj _ ih =>\\n    rw [SimpleGraph.Walk.length_cons]\\n    exact mem_ballWithin_succ_of_adj G _ _ _ _ ih hadj.symm\"","StartLine":"33","TargetContent":"\"lemma mem_ballWithin_of_walk_reverse {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V] (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj]\\n    {v w : V} (q : G.Walk w v) : w ∈ GraphCalc.ballWithin G q.length v := by\\n  induction q with\\n  | nil =>\\n    rw [ballWithin_zero, SimpleGraph.Walk.length_nil]\\n    exact Finset.mem_singleton_self v\\n  | cons hadj q' ih =>\\n    rw [SimpleGraph.Walk.length_cons]\\n    exact mem_ballWithin_succ_of_adj G q'.length v _ w ih hadj.symm\"","TargetFile":"\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_2a2555cc/Challenge_2a2555cc.lean\"","toolAction":"\"Editing file\"","toolSummary":"\"Fix mem_ballWithin_of_walk_reverse in Challenge_2a2555cc.lean\""}}]}
