{"step_index":129,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:34:29Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-12T01:34:29+02:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-12T01:34:29+02:00\nFile Path: `file:///mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_2a2555cc/scratch.lean`\nTotal Lines: 41\nTotal Bytes: 1390\nShowing lines 1 to 41\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: import Mathlib\n2: import LeanProject.GraphInvariantsComputable\n3: \n4: lemma finset_min_getD_le {s : Finset ℕ} {b : ℕ} (hb : b ∈ s) :\n5:     s.min.getD 0 ≤ b := by\n6:   have h : s.min ≤ WithTop.some b := Finset.inf_le hb\n7:   cases hm : s.min with\n8:   | top =>\n9:     rw [hm] at h\n10:     simp at h\n11:   | coe m =>\n12:     rw [hm] at h\n13:     exact WithTop.coe_le_coe.mp h\n14: \n15: lemma radius_le_eccentricity {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\n16:     (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (v : V) :\n17:     GraphCalc.radius G ≤ GraphCalc.eccentricity G v := by\n18:   apply finset_min_getD_le\n19:   apply Finset.mem_image.mpr\n20:   exact ⟨v, Finset.mem_univ v, rfl⟩\n21: \n22: lemma finset_min_getD_le_of_mem (n : ℕ) {s : Finset ℕ} {b : ℕ} (hb : b ∈ s) :\n23:     s.min.getD n ≤ b := by\n24:   have h : s.min ≤ WithTop.some b := Finset.inf_le hb\n25:   cases hm : s.min with\n26:   | top =>\n27:     rw [hm] at h\n28:     simp at h\n29:   | coe m =>\n30:     rw [hm] at h\n31:     exact WithTop.coe_le_coe.mp h\n32: \n33: lemma eccentricity_le_of_ballWithin_eq_univ {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\n34:     (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (v : V) (k : ℕ)\n35:     (hkle : k ≤ Fintype.card V) (heq : GraphCalc.ballWithin G k v = Finset.univ) :\n36:     GraphCalc.eccentricity G v ≤ k := by\n37:   dsimp [GraphCalc.eccentricity, GraphCalc.minUpTo]\n38:   apply finset_min_getD_le_of_mem (Fintype.card V)\n39:   rw [Finset.mem_filter, Finset.mem_range]\n40:   exact ⟨Nat.lt_succ_of_le hkle, heq⟩\n41: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
{"step_index":130,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:34:29Z","thinking":"**Analyzing `finset_min_getD_le` Lemma**\n\nThe goal is to understand and potentially use the lemma `finset_min_getD_le`. This lemma asserts that for a finite set of natural numbers and an element `b` in the set, the minimum element of the set, defaulted to 0 if the set is empty, is less than or equal to `b`.\n\nThe proof uses `Finset.inf_le` to establish that the minimum is less than or equal to `WithTop.some b`. The proof handles the case where the minimum is `top` (representing the empty set, in this context, or that there's no minimum) separately. The `coe` case uses the fact that `WithTop.coe_le_coe.mp` holds. This appears to correctly prove the statement.\n\nThe lemma seems useful for relating an element of the set to the set's smallest element.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/tools/antigravity/check.sh scratch.lean\"","Cwd":"\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_2a2555cc\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"10000","toolAction":"\"Running command\"","toolSummary":"\"Run check.sh on scratch.lean\""}}]}
